{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak","id":1483900,"title":"Are Vampires WEAK?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-13T12:50:40-07:00","id":1483900,"title":"Are Vampires WEAK?","content":"There's a thread in the VtM forums about crossovers using V20/Revised editions and someone there mentioned this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire PCs are expected to start the game way too &quot;lame&quot; for their kind, as one friend once put it to me &quot;You can't even FEEL like a TRUE vampire with 3 dots in disciplines and everybody around you and their mother is more powerful than you&quot; and I'd say he's not really wrong. The perception is that the PCs in Vampire are so vulnerable and weak that it's really hard not to feel damned while you can't see the sun anymore and still you can barely overcome a normal human in overall strength. Just imagine if Mage PC's started with only 2-3 dots in spheres and/or you had mostly only access to perception powers, it sure would feel different, but instead, Mages start with 6 dots in spheres, they're probably not that impressive for their kind, but still, they can definitely FEEL like real mages, the same thing is true for Werewolves, to start they begin with the powers associated to werewolves from legends, (I'd say even much more so, as werewolves in WoD are clearly superior to the general werewolf from legends, as WoD is the only universe I know where werewolves are the &quot;best fighters in the world&quot;) they can change form at will, etc, so they don't really depend on Gifts, Gifts for werewolves are just pluses, now imagine if the only feature starting werewolves PCs had was being vulnerable to silver and then they'd be closer to what the average PC feels when starting a vampire game. </div> </div> </div>I know now he's referring to OWoD, but because I'm working on a VtR chronicle where Vampire PCs may (well, eventually will) bump into other monsters, I want to make sure; are Vampires weak? It's one thing to not be a combat train like Uratha or to not have the sheer versatility of Willworkers, but does that really make them &quot;lame?&quot; If I throw the Coterie at Werewolves, Magi, Changelings, etc, is there a likely chance they'll feel outclassed and want to play another splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:23:02-07:00","id":1483905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak#post1483900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a thread in the VtM forums about crossovers using V20/Revised editions and someone there mentioned this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know now he's referring to OWoD, but because I'm working on a VtR chronicle where Vampire PCs may (well, eventually will) bump into other monsters, I want to make sure; are Vampires weak? It's one thing to not be a combat train like Uratha or to not have the sheer versatility of Willworkers, but does that really make them &quot;lame?&quot; If I throw the Coterie at Werewolves, Magi, Changelings, etc, is there a likely chance they'll feel outclassed and want to play another splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, simply put, vampires are the most PHYSICAL strong major splat.<br /> The 3 main reasons are:<br /> -everyone of them starts with the Physical intensity innate ability, for every blood point spent you can add 2 dice to a physical action.<br /> As your Blood potency increases, the ability to spend multiple blood points per turn gives you a great edge.<br /> -Any vampire can learn without instructor Vigor (dots adds to Strenght), Resilience (dots adds to Stamina) and Celerity (dots adds to Defence).<br /> They cap at five dots, but extra levels can raise the relative attribute above the character normal cap.<br /> -And as an emergency tactic, when they frenzy they add Blood potency to all Physical rolls and desistances, plus they ignore wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Consider that the 3 mechanics above cumulates....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:31:16-07:00","id":1483906,"title":"","content":"First or second edition?<br /> <br /> First edition Requiem came at the very beginning of nWoD feeling out where to balance supernatural powers in the context of trying to avoid oWoD's moments of excess and plan ahead to put the main three splats in a comparable ballpark. The end result is that compared to where the gamelines were later on, Requiem vampires felt a little muted and conservatively designed, aside from the customary strengths of White Wolf vampires (the Vinculum was always a potent tool in your pocket) and a few balancing blips that didn't reflect where later rules went (1e Protean gave access to aggravated damage output much more easily than other 1e powersets doled it out).<br /> <br /> Second edition Requiem does a pretty good job of spreading out useful Discipline powers so that even the first dot of a core Discipline feels meaningful and transforms what your character can do, I would say. Stuff like Iron Edict and Face in the Crowd is pretty versatile and effective, and neither of them eat up all three of your starting dots to get.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:35:03-07:00","id":1483907,"title":"","content":"I speak mostly from theory here. I only storyguided Mummy, Hunter and Mage. I read as many books I can put my hands on and a lot of Storyteller Vault, I also have SOME experience with Demon, Changeling, Deviant, Werewolf and Vampire from using them as NPCs is the Mage Chronicle.<br /> <br /> With all this information, I really suspect that Vampires are at the bottom of Supernatural Food Chain. At same level of Changelings on my opinion.<br /> <br /> This not make them lame, but make crossover interaction more complex. Mages can do things others splats dream about and Werewolves in combat form are nearly immortal recovering all non-agg wounds per round. <br /> <br /> Vampires thrive on other things and crossover interaction need to highlight this. Mages can't do magic in front of mortals without consequences and Acts of Hubris when a Vampire can use Disciplines in front of a crowd without fear of destroying the space-time. Werewolves on combat form are savages capable of killing friends and can't use it's full capacity outside of combat. Vampires are more reliable and capable of work with fewer limitations.<br /> <br /> This have narrative highlight also. Vampires have more connection with humanity to the point they miss being human. Werewolves, Mages, Changelings and Mummies are less capable to interact because human feel so weird to their understanding and experiences. Mages know the truth and can't care less about questions of souls and logical functions, Werewolves have more understanding of spirits than human society, even Changelings need to be aware of Fae creatures and Clarity, keeping the Freehold working also, instead of create community with other humans. Vampires go to parties, have sex and don't have any other great social impediment than being pseudo-incapable of working at day.<br /> <br /> This, still, is a opinion from theory and not so much experience. Seems like creatures like Geist also have the upsides of Vampire without the downsides, but I don't finish that books yet. But my analysis let me to this conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:41:31-07:00","id":1483909,"title":"","content":"If we were talking CofD 1e... I think there might be a point that the starting level package was too weak for where the CofD settled on things... but that's why vampires got a buff in 2e to bring them more in-line with everyone else. The 2e innate powers are more impressive, the drawbacks are slower to kick in, and so on.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> There's a significant difference between &quot;are starting level characters balanced against each other from different splats&quot; something the CofD is not too concerned with, vs &quot;are vampires as a whole underwhelming compared to everyone else out there.&quot; There's a lot of things that make vampires scary that tends to be more NPC material than starting PC material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-13-2022, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:45:40-07:00","id":1483910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483906#post1483906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First or second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Edition. As much as I preferred the fluff for Carthians and the Crone in the First Edition, my one and only Chronicle there... Didn't turn out well.<br /> <br /> Not saying it was the Edition's fault (it <b>was</b> the first and so far, only WoD chronicle I GM'ed) but the 2nd Edition was the first time I ever heard anything <b>nice</b> about VtR. Before that, everyone I knew seemed to look at Requiem like it was New Coke.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:48:19-07:00","id":1483912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483905#post1483905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, simply put, vampires are the most PHYSICAL strong major splat.<br /> The 3 main reasons are:<br /> -Every one of them starts with the Physical intensity innate ability, for every blood point spent you can add 2 dice to a physical action.<br /> As your Blood potency increases, the ability to spend multiple blood points per turn gives you a great edge.<br /> -Any vampire can learn without instructor Vigor (dots adds to Strenght), Resilience (dots adds to Stamina), and Celerity (dots adds to Defence).<br /> They cap at five dots, but extra levels can raise the relative attribute above the character's normal cap.<br /> -And as an emergency tactic, when they frenzy they add Blood potency to all Physical rolls and resistances, plus they ignore wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Consider that the 3 mechanics above cumulate....</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I was expecting the Werewolves to have the Physical edge. Interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:49:57-07:00","id":1483913,"title":"","content":"Lets see, they have the inherent ability to degrade lethal and aggravated damage one tier from most non-supernatural sources. They get a passive bonus to Defense with Celerity and can defend from firearms, this is when they are not using it to interrupt the opponent's flow with precise actions.<br /> <br /> Then we have Resilience, which is ridiculously powerful. It degrades damage from EVERYTHING for the entire turn for a mere point of vitae. The mage's aggravated damage spell, the werewolf's claws, the 200 people firing squad and the rocket launcher. Plus with enough skill in Vigor, a peak human condition vampire can throw something with enough force that even a vampire will take lethal damage (size 10+ objects) and with more force than being hit by lightning. That will certainly make enough of an impression that foes will reconsider their chances of survival.<br /> <br /> This is all provided that the vampire even choses to entertain their....guests. Dominate, Nightmare and Majesty can simply shut down targets in combat and are very useful outside of it. The its all a matter of feeding them vitae to start forging a Vinculum. One drink makes &quot;diplomacy&quot; much easier and sets up the second drink, placing a powerful supernatural under their wing.<br /> <br /> This does not mean they have carte blanche. Sure, mages are much less deadly when taken by surprise. But mages are also dirty cheats and masters of asymmetrical combat. A veteran one will probably have prepared more than a few contingencies on hand at all times or can come up with a spell that seizes the advantage for them. Werewolves may be just as resilient as vampires, but they can be even more ferocious and, unlike vampires, they are designed to master pack tactics, which is a significant force multiplier to an already powerful foe.<br /> <br /> Vampires still need to strategize and prepare, but they are by no means weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-13-2022, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T15:12:16-07:00","id":1483922,"title":"","content":"There's a thing that bears knowing about vampires that's present in other lines to some degree without as much of an explicit metaphysical focus toward it, which is this: the Requiem is about finding, building, and exploiting a niche. In between struggling with Humanity and hiding from the sun, the thing that vampires do is carve out a space in the local ecosystem (literal or metaphorical) and use the tools they have as unliving feedback loops for distilled Life to allow themselves to carry on in as safe, comfortable, and rewarding a fashion as they prefer.<br /> <br /> That means extending their reach, painting as much of the town as they can in their particular shade of red, and generally getting to the point where you have a territory under control enough that where your next meal is coming from isn't a primary concern. From there, you can step up the Maslow hierarchy to pursue more personal goals like communion with Old Gods, or safeguarding cursed relics, or transcending the limits of vampirism, or twisting new ideas from the living to serve the purposes of dead, or just making yourself politically irreplaceable from all the things you bring to the table.<br /> <br /> That <i>also</i> means being out of juice has a markedly more direct impact on the Kindred than it does on, say, werewolves or mages or the Created. The downside to having a theoretically infinite ceiling on what you can get under your control with enough blood and servants and allies is that you're the cardinal point of vulnerability in the whole machine you've built, which necessarily requires that vampires be vulnerable in a way mummies and changelings and the Bound are not.<br /> <br /> Vampire is arguably the monster game most concerned with inhabiting and twisting the mortal sphere as an entity, and its primary driving impetus for doing so is that undercurrent of hunger and desperation that the Kindred carry through their nights.<br /> <br /> (It's also worth noting that a lot of things in ChroD that cause a monster to more closely resemble its legendary basis are <i>failstates</i> \u2014 the easiest point of comparison I can provide is that Uratha who tilt their Harmony too high look more like movie werewolves than werewolves who belong to packs and tribes and engage with the Shadow do. The Kindred partake of iconic vampiric strengths and engage in dramatic emotional setpieces because that's the type of game this is, but maintaining Humanity specifically helps keep you from being something physically incapable of crossing a line of salt or routinely gets pincushioned by foot-long wooden spikes instead of being able to credibly pretend to be a a person with vampirism, and the slow slide down the ladder with age is as much a matter of compromise as fatigue. You start out not looking like a legendary vampire because being a legendary vampire is <i>exhausting</i> or <i>overwhelming</i> for people who grew up as people.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T21:27:41-07:00","id":1483953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483912#post1483912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, I was expecting the Werewolves to have the Physical edge. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that werewolves have surely the physical edge as starting characters, but vampires can use experience to vastly increase their puissance, while werewolves have a couple of gift about that but no more.<br /> It must be said that i m considering only the highest potential pool of dices, every splat has specific advantages and useful powers that can turn the result of a battle upside down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T21:52:25-07:00","id":1483956,"title":"","content":"This is also something where you can't just look at single starting level PCs. The CofD (and 2e even more so) reduced the stress on werewolves as the physical powerhouse measuring stick for the game-line. What makes the Uratha scary is their exceptional teamwork boosting. A lone vampires vs. a lone werewolf isn't the massive advantage for the werewolf it is in the WoD, and really comes down to a more individual level than innate powers. A coterie of vampires vs. a pack of werewolves is much more stacked in the werewolves' favor because they have a lot more stuff that's oriented around boosting their effectiveness as pack hunters. A coterie can, of course, be a well trained combat unit, but that takes a lot of specific training compared to what a pack gets just for being a pack of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T23:12:47-07:00","id":1483963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483953#post1483953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It must be said that I'm considering only the highest potential pool of dice, every splat has specific advantages and useful powers that can turn the result of a battle upside down</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the rant that inspired this thread, it sounded like the original author was only considering <i>dots</i>. He compared the Vampire's dots in Disciplines to the Mage's dots in Spheres. I actually tried to make similar comparisons myself with the 2nd Edition ChoD books, but I stopped because it was taking forever to write (and the comparison did not work with Werewolf at <i>all</i>).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T01:34:50-07:00","id":1483973,"title":"","content":"2ed vampires are all but weak. On raw numbers are probably the best major splat (probably not from the beginning though). Let's analyze a bit more in depth:<br /> <br /> - at low BP (1, 2 or 3) probably - on a physical point of view only - werewolves can have an edge on vampires, and yet it's the only splat which is outperforming kindred on raw physical power. Non the less when talking about mental discipline kindred outperform any other splat. Plus a good use of Animalism can compensate the gap in terms of dice/damage<br /> <br /> - at BP 5 the gap goes away: maximizing the physical stats lead both werewolves and kindred to a pool of 28 dice (more or less) without counting devotions like force of nature, sudden strength etc.<br /> <br /> - Above BP 5 kindred have the edge on any other splat in terms of raw numbers - due to physical intensity and frenzy.<br /> <br /> And again, this is only if you talk about physical stats. Kindred are very versatile and can easily turns their enemies against each other: Majesty, Dominate, Animalism 4.<br /> <br /> Any encounter is very situational but I would say that, no, kindred are not weak at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-14-2022, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T04:35:50-07:00","id":1483977,"title":"","content":"I will start by saying that comparing anything to mages is a futile endevour since they are OP by design and that is ok, lines are not meant to be balanced, regarding vampires in requiem they are not weak at all and they are, as a matter of fact, one of the potentially more destructive splats from a purely physical standpoint, a vamp beating an uratha to death with their bare hands is very much a possibility here unlike WoD, what puts them at the bottom of the supernatural food chain are their crippling weaknesses and the fact that they have very few ways to interact with ephemerals, you can be the baddest elder out there but if someone (even a human) manage to get access to your haven during the day while you are sleeping then you are dead and spirits and ghosts are very good at finding out secrets...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T04:39:08-07:00","id":1483978,"title":"","content":"Another thing that penalizes vampires is their extremely slow progression, unlike the other splats, their triggers for beats are extremely self destructive in nature (frenzies and degenerations roll) so most players will tend to avoid them unlike werewolves for example that get a ton of beats from all the various positive conditions they can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T04:59:35-07:00","id":1483979,"title":"","content":"I think the other thing to look at is not comparative, but in absolute terms: just as starting-character Mages /feel/ wizardly, do starting-character vampires /feel/ like playing a scary cool vampire? <br /> <br /> My test for this is, can a starting character Vampire feel like it's the monster in a horror movie. And I think they definitely can. Even before we get to Disciplines, a starting vampire is tougher, faster, and stronger (Physical Intensity), can see you in the dark (Kindred Senses), can heal from all but the most grievous wounds (Healing), and can make you do things that you wouldn't otherwise (Predatory Aura). <br /> <br /> Once you get to Disciplines, the horror-monster vibes escalate. They know about the holy water in your flask before you even reach for it - maybe the rats in your walls whispered your secrets to them. They disappear into a crowd, or sink into the earth. Your mind is theirs. Your /want/ to be theirs. Now, it can sometimes take some clever GMing to allow these weaker powers to have their moments to shine, but give a player the opportunity to use a one-dot power to great effect and vampires don't feel disappointingly weak at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T07:52:08-07:00","id":1483985,"title":"","content":"IMO, Vamps have 3 LARGE advantages:<br /> 1) OP social desciplines <br /> 2) couple of pretty OP combos <br /> 3) Atributes boost for blood.<br /> <br /> For CofD IMO, Vampires, Werewolves and Geists are more or less on the same level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:07:20-07:00","id":1484008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483973#post1483973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2ed vampires are all but weak. On raw numbers are probably the best major splat (probably not from the beginning though). Let's analyze a bit more in depth:<br /> <br /> - at low BP (1, 2 or 3) probably - on a physical point of view only - werewolves can have an edge on vampires, and yet it's the only splat which is outperforming kindred on raw physical power. Non the less when talking about mental discipline kindred outperform any other splat. Plus a good use of Animalism can compensate the gap in terms of dice/damage<br /> <br /> - at BP 5 the gap goes away: maximizing the physical stats lead both werewolves and kindred to a pool of 28 dice (more or less) without counting devotions like force of nature, sudden strength etc.<br /> <br /> - Above BP 5 kindred have the edge on any other splat in terms of raw numbers - due to physical intensity and frenzy.<br /> <br /> And again, this is only if you talk about physical stats. Kindred are very versatile and can easily turns their enemies against each other: Majesty, Dominate, Animalism 4.<br /> <br /> Any encounter is very situational but I would say that, no, kindred are not weak at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am curious about how they get to 28 dice, could you please provide more details ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:24:05-07:00","id":1484012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484008#post1484008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious about how they get to 28 dice, could you please provide more details ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength 5 + Skill 5 + Vigor 5 + 10 dice from Physical Intensity + 3 dice from Willpower, most likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:28:48-07:00","id":1484013,"title":"","content":"While I think comparing the power levels of the various games in CofD is an exercise in futility, I do think a lot of people confuse simplicity for lack of power when it comes to vampires. As previously mentioned, every Discipline does exactly what it is supposed to straight from the first dot, and not in any half-measures. Beyond the first dot, Disciplines are all straightforward, uncomplicated, and focused, even if the focus of, say, Animalism is not actually what is expected. And because each Discipline is relatively cheap and very good at what it does, players are constantly using them to solve problems, at least ime. Something about a hammer and everything looking like nails.<br /> <br /> And, actually, I want to elaborate more on their powers being cheap, because it comes in two flavors. First, the first dot of basically every Discipline is free, or conditionally free. Vampires can just do that whenever they like, at no cost. Some Disciplines even do not have a Vitae cost until the third or fourth dot! Second, blood is cheap, or at least, it can be, and only the fifth dot of any given Discipline is going to add a Willpower cost [and when they do, the benefits are usually worth it]. This gives vampires lots of leeway to just use their powers which only mages, beasts, demons, and some deviants can match. Except, by having such a focused and powerful list of abilities, the vampire is paradoxically less likely to have a power that will not solve or bypass the story's current problem entirely.<br /> <br /> Basically, the vampire toolkit is built on exerting control, and every Discipline is among the best powers in the various games at exacting its flavor of control, imo. And if your players feel like they are missing out on the potential versatility of other games' powers, well, that is what Devotions are for [or the blood bond/ghouling if they like their vampires bastardly].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:46:15-07:00","id":1484016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483978#post1483978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that penalizes vampires is their extremely slow progression, unlike the other splats, their triggers for beats are extremely self destructive in nature (frenzies and degenerations roll) so most players will tend to avoid them unlike werewolves for example that get a ton of beats from all the various positive conditions they can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another thing about points of comparison.<br /> <br /> For example, most splats don't get free Power Stat increases without XP over time, and they can't eat their own kind for more XP either.<br /> <br /> Sure, most people sitting down and playing VtR, or playing a mixed CofD chronicle, aren't going to cover a long enough period of time for that to matter for PCs, but in the setting at large vampires can get power just by surviving long enough. VtR is also far less &quot;kill all Diablerists on sight,&quot; than VtM is, and makes detecting them in the first place harder (no more needing to buy special things to hide it from Auspex 2, and Auspex is now a Clan signature Discipline instead of a common one anyway).<br /> <br /> So yeah, since the PCs are unlikely to get the chance to spend 100 years being Dialberie addicts before &quot;seeing the light&quot; and switching to the LeS or OD to cure them of their addiction (sincerely or not it doesn't really matter) to easily net ~75 XP (including costs to keep Humanity up) more than most splats would get without having to go through a Beat loop (plus if they get the Addicted condition for Diablerie they also get a Beat loop to exploit out of it as well), it can feel &quot;weak.&quot; But the setting itself has plenty of vampires that took a short cut to impressive supernatural power (at least by the standards of immortal creatures).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483979#post1483979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the other thing to look at is not comparative, but in absolute terms: just as starting-character Mages /feel/ wizardly, do starting-character vampires /feel/ like playing a scary cool vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this test is really hard because... who's idea of what that means? A 0 XP neonate vampire isn't going to be David from the Lost Boys, they're going to be Michael. Or at least one of the lackey vampires that's gotten a bit more skill under their belts without being as powerful as David. You could do the same with Near Dark, etc.<br /> <br /> Going back farther Lord Ruthven, Carmilla, and Varney are easily done as 0 XP vampires, while Count Dracula is way above what you're doing at 0 XP.<br /> <br /> One of the on-going problems with both Vampire lines, is that what a &quot;base-line&quot; vampire should be capable of is highly variable; but vampires are frequently shown as taking time to come into their full power. If people come into things expecting their &quot;cool scary vampire&quot; to only have been a vampire for a few years, it's a much lower bar than a few decades (part of the WoD's problem in 1e through V20 is that very assumption that starting level vampires have had a fairly significant time as fledglings, where VtR and V5 orient things such that 0XP starting characters are expecting to be much younger vampires so their power level is more in-line with expectations).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:59:27-07:00","id":1484018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484012#post1484012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength 5 + Skill 5 + Vigor 5 + 10 dice from Physical Intensity + 3 dice from Willpower, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since that vampire can use 10 vitae per turn, that implies a Blood Potency of 10. Given that the constrain posted was maxed stats and assuming we are trying to maximize damage, I think the resulting calculation would be:<br /> <br /> 10 (Strength) + 10 (Skill) + 5 (passive bonus from Vigor) + 9 (maximum amount of Physical Intensity - 1 BP already used to activate Vigor as a damage bonus) + 3 Willpower = 37<br /> <br /> Which means 37 hit dice, where each hit does [weapon damage] + 5 (Vigor's active bonus). Which means that if the maxed vampire is wiling to use 13% of their max blood pool in a single attack (so theoretically they can do this at most 7 times before requiring some downtime to refill it), they can bring forth one an incredible amount of force on the fly. But this is provided that they do not need to divert resources in things like chase after their target, interrupt enemy actions via Celerity or resist a deadly barrage via Protean. But still, its very impressive amount of consistent power, especially considering that things like targeted attacks, fighting styles and Devotions are yet to be accounted for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-14-2022, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:02:56-07:00","id":1484019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484012#post1484012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength 5 + Skill 5 + Vigor 5 + 10 dice from Physical Intensity + 3 dice from Willpower, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>+ 5 frenzy also <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:07:42-07:00","id":1484022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484018#post1484018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since that vampire can use 10 vitae per turn, that implies a Blood Potency of 10. Given that the constrain posted was maxed stats and assuming we are trying to maximize damage, I think the resulting calculation would be:<br /> <br /> 10 (Strength) + 10 (Skill) + 5 (passive bonus from Vigor) + 9 (maximum amount of Physical Intensity - 1 BP already used to activate Vigor as a damage bonus) + 3 Willpower = 37<br /> <br /> Which means 37 hit dice, where each hit does [weapon damage] + 5 (Vigor's active bonus). Which means that if the maxed vampire is wiling to use 13% of their max blood pool in a single attack (so theoretically they can do this at most 7 times before requiring some downtime to refill their blood pool), they can bring forth one an incredible amount of force on the fly. But this is provided that they do not need to divert resources in things like chase after their target, interrupt enemy actions via Celerity or resist a deadly barrage via Protean. But still, its very impressive considering that things like targeted attacks, fighting styles and Devotions are yet to be accounted for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. 1 vitae gives you +2 in an attribute.<br /> <br /> So with BP 5 you can have:<br /> <br /> 5 str + 5 vig + 5 skill + 5 BP frenzy + 8 for using 4 vitae for physical intensity and still remain 1 vitae to activate vigor.<br /> <br /> At BP 10, maximizing everything just for the sake of play who has it bigger, you can reach:<br /> <br /> Str 10 + skill 10 + Vigor 5 + 18 physical intensity (9 vitae) + 10 BP (frenzy) = 53. You can consider also protean 4 to get another+4 on the grab roll = 57. And with Force of Nature you can move another 10-15 points to strength...<br /> <br /> Also, I think vampires have one of the most broken combat power: swarm form: you roll the whole pool - included disciplines - ignoring defense and armor and taking only 1 or 2 damages per attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-14-2022, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:09:08-07:00","id":1484024,"title":"","content":"I think even on an individual level werewolves end up with some impressive powers, just where the emphasis is not so much on continuous physical enhancements as it is leveraging certain advantages (and depriving those of an enemy) that let them shape a scenario into chasing a target into a corner before charging at them in the war form (possibly with some enhancements).<br /> <br /> Although it also put a lot of Uratha advantages into Merits rather than Gifts, which I think is okay but does make it a bit tricky for me to keep track of what you can build one to be capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:39:05-07:00","id":1484027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483973#post1483973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2ed vampires are all but weak. On raw numbers are probably the best major splat (probably not from the beginning though). Let's analyze a bit more in depth:<br /> <br /> - at low BP (1, 2 or 3) probably - on a physical point of view only - werewolves can have an edge on vampires, and yet it's the only splat which is outperforming kindred on raw physical power. Non the less when talking about mental discipline kindred outperform any other splat. Plus a good use of Animalism can compensate the gap in terms of dice/damage<br /> <br /> - at BP 5 the gap goes away: maximizing the physical stats lead both werewolves and kindred to a pool of 28 dice (more or less) without counting devotions like force of nature, sudden strength etc.<br /> <br /> - Above BP 5 kindred have the edge on any other splat in terms of raw numbers - due to physical intensity and frenzy.<br /> <br /> And again, this is only if you talk about physical stats. Kindred are very versatile and can easily turns their enemies against each other: Majesty, Dominate, Animalism 4.<br /> <br /> Any encounter is very situational but I would say that, no, kindred are not weak at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to derail this too much, but from what I've seen Werewolves have the edge over Vampires at any amount of exp. The highest dice pool I was able to get for a BP 5 Vampire was 27 with 9-again using force of nature (only on grapple attacks though). They could boost this up to 37 with physical intensity but only had the vitae to do this for two turns. This Vampire cost 69 exp to build.<br /> <br /> I compared this against the best PU 5 Werewolf I could make and while the Werewolf's dice pool was variable due to Crimson Spasm being a roll, it averaged at 37 dice (with 8-again) and could go all the way up into the 40s (the dice pool for Crimson Spasm was 24, so I took 7 as the average number of successes). This could last up to 18 turns, and the Werewolf had other notable advantages such as a health pool in Gauru of 22 (good luck overcoming that regeneration). To top it all off this Werewolf only cost 41 exp to build.<br /> <br /> Naturally achieving these numbers in either case requires a good deal of chicanery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:52:38-07:00","id":1484030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484027#post1484027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to derail this too much, but from what I've seen Werewolves have the edge over Vampires at any amount of exp. The highest dice pool I was able to get for a BP 5 Vampire was 27 with 9-again using force of nature (only on grapple attacks though). They could boost this up to 37 with physical intensity but only had the vitae to do this for two turns. This Vampire cost 69 exp to build.<br /> <br /> I compared this against the best PU 5 Werewolf I could make and while the Werewolf's dice pool was variable due to Crimson Spasm being a roll, it averaged at 37 dice (with 8-again) and could go all the way up into the 40s (the dice pool for Crimson Spasm was 24, so I took 7 as the average number of successes). This could last up to 18 turns, and the Werewolf had other notable advantages such as a health pool in Gauru of 22 (good luck overcoming that regeneration). To top it all off this Werewolf only cost 41 exp to build.<br /> <br /> Naturally achieving these numbers in either case requires a good deal of chicanery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b><u>Vampire Blood potency 5</u></b><b>:</b><br /> Strength 5 + Brawl 5 + BP 5 + Vigor 5 + 8 (4 vitae on strength) = 28 dice (+4 protean = 32)<br /> - force of nature for a + 8 dice more = 40 dice<br /> - swarm form: roll full pool ignoring defense and taking only 1 or max 2 damages per attack.<br /> - can do aggravated with protean 4 and 1 merit ignoring the werewolf regeneration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Werewolf Primal Urge 5</u></b><b>:</b><br /> Strength 5 (+3 in Gauru 8) + Brawl 5 + Purity 5 + Crimson Spasm (stamina + survival - the 8'again does not come here - is 12 dice with an average of 4/5 successes which means 10 dice more on the attack) 10= 28 dice<br /> - they have the 8' again which is a great plus, I agree.<br /> <br /> How did you get 24 dice for crimson? Crimson is Survival+Stamina. Stamina is 7 at max and survival is 5. 8'again here is not applicable. on an average roll it gives you 8 to 10 dices more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T13:01:52-07:00","id":1484032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484027#post1484027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to derail this too much, but from what I've seen Werewolves have the edge over Vampires at any amount of exp. The highest dice pool I was able to get for a BP 5 Vampire was 27 with 9-again using the force of nature (only on grapple attacks though). They could boost this up to 37 with physical intensity but only had the vitae to do this for two turns. This Vampire cost 69 exp to build.<br /> <br /> I compared this against the best PU 5 Werewolf I could make and while the Werewolf's dice pool was variable due to Crimson Spasm being a roll, it averaged at 37 dice (with 8-again) and could go all the way up into the 40s (the dice pool for Crimson Spasm was 24, so I took 7 as the average number of successes). This could last up to 18 turns, and the Werewolf had other notable advantages such as a health pool in Gauru of 22 (good luck overcoming that regeneration). To top it all off this Werewolf only cost 41 exp to build.<br /> <br /> Naturally achieving these numbers, in either case, requires a good deal of chicanery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of chicanery and Werewolves, I found this video through Twitter about a Storyteller who set up an ambush by Uratha. It... Did not go as he planned. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zbFsIYCnKt4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zbFsIYCnKt4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zbFsIYCnKt4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/zbFsIYCnKt4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:22:52-07:00","id":1484040,"title":"","content":"Speaking of oWoD: in a long run Vampires were one of the strongest splats (look at Mithra or Yaga) while Garou was the weakest one (at least lore-wise - no exampke if Garou, of whatever Ranm, defeated Mathuail - - even though it's posdible mechanicaly).<br /> <br /> Also: may we compare Vampires with not-werewolves for ONCE?! Let's compare vampires with... Beasts. No one like Beasts.<br /> <br /> P.P.S: For high levels, the best Uratha veapon - Elemental gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 06-14-2022, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:38:18-07:00","id":1484043,"title":"","content":"I like Beasts.<br /> <br /> But that aside, one of the problems with comparing different CofD game lines is that some are very specific, and some are very modular. Comparing vampires and begotten is hard because Beast is a more variable-at-base game. The &quot;innate&quot; package is much more flexible. The same with Changeling and Deviant. You can't really compare well without significantly short-changing one side or the other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:40:06-07:00","id":1484044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484043#post1484043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Beasts.<br /> <br /> But that aside, one of the problems with comparing different CofD game lines is that some are very specific, and some are very modular. Comparing vampires and begotten is hard because Beast is a more variable-at-base game. The &amp;quot;innate&amp;quot; package is much more flexible. The same with Changeling and Deviant. You can't really compare well without significantly short-changing one side or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, what about Sin-Eaters? Anyone but werewolves, for God sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:44:41-07:00","id":1484045,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm having trouble getting my head around Beasts. I'm not sure what they bring that Changelings couldn't. <br /> <br /> If we're tired of comparing Vampires to Werewolves, we can always compare them to Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T14:54:29-07:00","id":1484046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484030#post1484030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>Werewolf Primal Urge 5</u></b><b>:</b><br /> Strength 5 (+3 in Gauru 8) + Brawl 5 + Purity 5 + Crimson Spasm (stamina + survival - the 8'again does not come here - is 12 dice with an average of 4/5 successes which means 10 dice more on the attack) 10= 28 dice<br /> - they have the 8' again which is a great plus, I agree.<br /> <br /> How did you get 24 dice for crimson? Crimson is Survival+Stamina. Stamina is 7 at max and survival is 5. 8'again here is not applicable. on an average roll it gives you 8 to 10 dices more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said there was a lot of chicanery.<br /> <br /> If you dig into the Werewolf merits you'll quickly find that the PU limits on attributes are at best guidelines. In this case to get 24 dice on the roll we have Stamina + Survival + Purity. Our stamina is 5 + 1 from favored form, +1 using totemic empowerment and +1 from either embodiment of the firstborn or the totem advantage. We'll activate the gift in either Urshul or Gauru for +2 stamina, bringing our stamina total to 10. We then add to that 5 Survival + 1 from totem advantages (so 6) plus 5 Purity plus willpower (3) gives us 24 dice total.<br /> <br /> Through similar chicanery our wolf has 6 brawl (plus area of expertise) and 7 strength going up to 8 in their favoured form (probably Gauru) before form bonuses. This all stacks along with the relevant Gifts to give us 24 dice as a base attack pool with however many successes * 2 extra dice from Crimson Spasm (I went with 7 as I said giving us 38).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484030#post1484030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Vampire Blood potency 5</u></b><b>:</b><br /> Strength 5 + Brawl 5 + BP 5 + Vigor 5 + 8 (4 vitae on strength) = 28 dice (+4 protean = 32)<br /> - force of nature for a + 8 dice more = 40 dice<br /> - swarm form: roll full pool ignoring defense and taking only 1 or max 2 damages per attack.<br /> - can do aggravated with protean 4 and 1 merit ignoring the werewolf regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a number of assumptions here I feel are unwarranted. For Force of Nature you've clearly assumed the Vampire has 5 Stamina and 5 Dex, I didn't assume this because it costs too much exp and the Vampire was already much more expensive than the Werewolf. If you want to spend another 12 exp getting the Vampire those attribute dots it puts him at 40 exp more expensive than the Werewolf and you have to reasonably start asking what the Werewolf is spending all that exp on (Tongue of Flame is always fun). And if you're going to be using force of nature, that that's 8 vitae and an instant action. Your BP 5 vampire only has 15 vitae and can only spend 5 per turn. In other words, that's 2 full turns before you can even start using the devotion, and then you need to spend <b>another</b> 2 instant actions to shift the dots around, and after all that you will only have 1 turn of full physical intensity blood boosting (assuming you spend blood on nothing else). I think it's fair to say that as your Vampire spends 4 turns &quot;powering up&quot; you're going to be absolutely eviscerated by the Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you're assuming a frenzy here. This I think is unwarranted. Vampires can't just choose to Frenzy (unlike Werewolves and Death Rage), and when they do Frenzy they can't choose what the Beast's goal is (and &quot;get the fuck away from the big Werewolf&quot; is more likely than &quot;attack suicidally&quot;). Even if we assume the Vampire is riding the wave, this can take several turns to activate and there's no guarantee that the check succeeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484030#post1484030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">swarm form: roll full pool ignoring defense and taking only 1 or max 2 damages per attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ignored Swarm form since it doesn't directly boost the Vampire's dice pools and that was what I was most interested in. If we're going down that route though, Tongue of Flame is a hard counter to Swarm form. Also if you think about it Grasp of Howling winds should be devastating to a Vampire in Swarm form but obviously that's getting into the realm of ST fiat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484030#post1484030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can do aggravated with protean 4 and 1 merit ignoring the werewolf regeneration.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty clear that you can either have claws of the unholy OR swarm form but not both at the same time. Claws of the Unholy also isn't free, it requires frenzy, which leads to the issues described above. Furthermore, if you take Claws of the Unholy, that means you are not taking advantage of Protean 4's Barbed Hands meaning you lose the + Protean to grappling pools (meaning you lose grapples against the Werewolf and it can auto grapple you on a normal attack roll whenever it wishes). Lastly you're doing + 0 agg damage with claws of the unholy. Once you account for defense etc (be prepared for the Werewolf to have at least 12 defense) and things like Berserker's Might, you're going to be dealing very little if any damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","user":"Aurumae","date":". 06-14-2022, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T15:04:10-07:00","id":1484047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484045#post1484045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm having trouble getting my head around Beasts. I'm not sure what they bring that Changelings couldn't. <br /> <br /> If we're tired of comparing Vampires to Werewolves, we can always compare them to Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>YESS!!! THIS!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T15:29:04-07:00","id":1484049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484045#post1484045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm having trouble getting my head around Beasts. I'm not sure what they bring that Changelings couldn't. </div> </div> </div> </div>From what I observed, the Begotten are essentially Thallain and/or Denizens from CtD, but with Kithain \u2018genes\u2019 that connect them much more firmly to humanity.<br /> <br /> The Lost, meanwhile, are more closer to the Wan Kuei than the Kithain. Except they escaped from Wonderland and Neverland instead of Hell, and aren\u2019t arbitrarily bound to a specific culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T15:39:24-07:00","id":1484050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484047#post1484047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> YESS!!! THIS!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe instead of turning this into a dogpile form of horseshit, we can meaningfully contribute with additional commentary.<br /> <br /> Or even better, though still very boring, maybe direct it to a thread where it's more relevant to the conversation, or create one for discussing the point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3201_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3201\" data-vbnamecard=\"3201\">Father Enoch</a> , on the subject of what Beast brings and how it differentiates from Changeling, if you'd like to take the conversation over to either of those forums, I'm sure the fanbase would be happy to help draw lines between the two.<br /> <br /> But let's keep the thread focused. At this point, do you still have lingering doubts or questions about vampires ability to act against other supernaturals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-14-2022, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:05:26-07:00","id":1484053,"title":"","content":"Please accept my apologies, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. Personally, I am more than satisfied with the input about how Vampires stack up to Mages (and yes, Werewolves too).<br /> <br /> This topic was very enlightening and I hope the original commenter who said (Masquerade) Vampires started out weak had a good look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:08:15-07:00","id":1484054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484053#post1484053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please accept my apologies, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. Personally, I am more than satisfied with the input about how Vampires stack up to Mages (and yes, Werewolves too).<br /> <br /> This topic was very enlightening and I hope the original commenter who said (Masquerade) Vampires started out weak had a good look.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to apologize, particularly to me. Just trying to keep on topic, while also being very tired of the tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:20:56-07:00","id":1484056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484054#post1484054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to apologize, particularly to me. Just trying to keep on topic, while also being very tired of the tangent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, too. <br /> Just... maybe , we can compare Vamps with someone other then werewolves. Sin-Eaters, why not? IIRC, they are the only splat which were nerfedin 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:38:53-07:00","id":1484061,"title":"","content":"Perhaps propose a comparison in question and how it's meant to apply to the issue of the relative strength of vampires?<br /> <br /> One of the reasons vampires vs. werewolves is some common in these things is that both are hunters. Vampires are like cats, they might live in communal social settings, but they tend to be solitary predators. Werewolves are... wolves. They live and hunt as a pack. That provides an arena of comparison: you can talk about how effective they are at their chose strategies and how the pros and cons of those strategies line up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Power&quot; is too vague in a vacuum. It needs context for a meaningful comparison.<br /> <br /> So, what do you wan to compare between vampires and sin-eaters?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:53:56-07:00","id":1484062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484053#post1484053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please accept my apologies, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. Personally, I am more than satisfied with the input about how Vampires stack up to Mages (and yes, Werewolves too).<br /> <br /> This topic was very enlightening and I hope the original commenter who said (Masquerade) Vampires started out weak had a good look.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the Arcana available and how creative the mage is, so the results can vary wildly. When approaching combat, I really like the combination of Time (with it you always have time to prepare and contingency spells ready) and Space (the mobility and range it offers lend themselves wonderfully to the asymmetrical combat tactics mages excel at):<br /> <br /> The mage just woke up. After a good night's sleep, she decided the vampire must be destroyed, she has way too much on her plate and the he will likely plot to strike at a critical time. <br /> <br /> Its morning, she knows the vampire will be sleeping away from any witnesses. She starts forming the rote for an Unmaking of Space. She uses his sympathetic name for a yantra, she can't be bothered to do more at the moment. The rote is one she created herself, which makes it a rote action. She does a quick mudra, adding +5 to the roll from her best skill. She Reaches for sensory range, then spends two mana, one for Time in a Bottle and another for Sympathetic Range. The spellcasting roll was an exceptional success (10 dice from Gnosis + 5 from Space + 5 from the yantra and with rote quality), there is no Withstand here, not from the connection or the vampire.<br /> <br /> Somewhere across town, the vampire suddenly has every piece of himself randomly dispersed across existence. With that 6 second task concluded, the mage goes to get some coffee and maybe a bagel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-14-2022, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:59:17-07:00","id":1484064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484061#post1484061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps propose a comparison in question and how it's meant to apply to the issue of the relative strength of vampires?<br /> <br /> One of the reasons vampires vs. werewolves is some common in these things is that both are hunters. Vampires are like cats, they might live in communal social settings, but they tend to be solitary predators. Werewolves are... wolves. They live and hunt as a pack. That provides an arena of comparison: you can talk about how effective they are at their chose strategies and how the pros and cons of those strategies line up.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Power&amp;quot; is too vague in a vacuum. It needs context for a meaningful comparison.<br /> <br /> So, what do you wan to compare between vampires and sin-eaters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say, for Geist with Psyche 5, what can s/he against BP5 Vampire, described above - in terms of direct fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:59:31-07:00","id":1484065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484045#post1484045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm having trouble getting my head around Beasts. I'm not sure what they bring that Changelings couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same fashion as vampires, changelings are built on a foundation of innate insecurity \u2014 Clarity means the Lost cannot be completely assured that their perceptions and worldview are appropriate to their truthful context, and gaining more power to repel predators makes it more likely that they will lose perspective and also attract more predatory or opportunistic attention. Clarity is closest to Integrity in what it represents, in that learning more about the supernatural events that made you a changeling imperils it (partially by making it easier to relive those events coincidentally), and gaining supernatural power brings you more vivid memory-dreams of those events. The primary benefit to high Clarity is too fragile to not be replaced by leaning into the development of magically-assisted senses to prop up one's flagging Perception pools, retreating to the Hedge, and getting their fix of human contact from dealing with other changelings.<br /> <br /> The Begotten don't have that problem. Their starting point as a monster involves knowing exactly what they are (in broad strokes, at least \u2014 further self-discovery is a major part of the splat's higher-level pursuits) and they have a place in the world set aside for them that's built to feed the dark desires they've acknowledged (which feed themselves, given enough time and power). The mild ego-trip of being a conscious piece of the world-soul making waves in the ocean of human thought shares narrative headspace with the Awakened's acts of blindness to such a degree that the main cultural element of Begotten society-such-as-it-is can be summarized as &quot;be mindful of the consequences of your actions, because the world is watching.&quot;<br /> <br /> Separately, even before 2e steered away from the specific angle of changelings as creatures of story, Beasts deal with narrative as a social instrument \u2014 the Lost of 1e sometimes encountered narrative enforcement at a personal level through dreams and talecrafting, but the Begotten's backyard is the place where the collective unconscious plays out stories that resonate with people in such a way that being in the Bright Realm of superhero fiction regularly arranges for characters to make choices that steer them toward being a hero or a villain and committing to or struggling with the role, and their most prominent unique antagonist type is fed on the cultural notions that You Gotta Kill Monsters Because Monsters Are Bad and can mobilize groups of people to prop them up in the starring role of the conflict that results from this.<br /> <br /> Where vampires and beasts have comparability is in their ability to mess with society at a large scale, but vampires need to build up a sociopolitical machine for that and beasts have a personal toolbox that is mostly hammers aside from persuading other monsters to lend their assistance on the strength of occult charisma. At that point, it gets a little abstract trying to pin down whether having a bloodline pumping Vitae into and out of guests at the local theme park to plant sleeper agent programming in their brains on the Ferris wheel is more or less influential than running a crew of Morlocks in the rafters of the local sports arena to spot petty criminals and contrive their public embarrassment so you can become a shadow-divinity of surveillance culture.<br /> <br /> (Cultural inertia aside, the reasons vampires and werewolves get compared a lot are pretty obvious: they're both territorial man-eating mainly-nocturnal predators of a fairly specific bent whose supernatural state causes them to occasionally flip out and murder people. You have to get into particular subtypes of the other monsters to get that close of a match. Beasts, changelings, and deviants are highly flexible splats, as HeavyArms correctly notes, along with mages and demons; mummies and Prometheans are specific in a form that isn't really comparable to vampires or werewolves, much as the Bound being very clearly Weird Ghosts isn't.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T17:36:32-07:00","id":1484068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484064#post1484064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say, for Geist with Psyche 5, what can s/he against BP5 Vampire, described above - in terms of direct fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>But what does this say about vampires? How is comparing tricked out combat stats useful if that's not the arena a vampire and a sin-eater are most likely to conflict in?<br /> <br /> This is why I noted the importance of vampires and werewolves hunting: up-close violence is the ultimate last resort of a hunter if they can't take prey in a safer manner. It's a skill vampires and werewolves need on a level.<br /> <br /> Sin-eaters don't need to fight like to fill their basest needs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T17:46:46-07:00","id":1484069,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure why Vampires and Sin Eaters would fight. <br /> <br /> Vampires and Werewolves both want the territory to hunt, even if for different prey. Vampires and Changelings both feed off people, even if in different ways. Magi want people to Awaken, which they can't do if they get turned into Vampires (they also really dig uncovering mysteries and Vampires like having their mystery, thank you, Gandalf). I thought Gheist was mostly about helping Wraiths move on.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a Vampire being responsible for the creation of one or two of the ghosts that seek out Gheists, but not all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:00:15-07:00","id":1484071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484069#post1484069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure why Vampires and Sin Eaters would fight.<br /> <br /> Vampires and Werewolves both want the territory to hunt, even if for different prey. Vampires and Changelings both feed off people, even if in different ways. Magi want people to Awaken, which they can't do if they get turned into Vampires (they also really dig uncovering mysteries and Vampires like having their mystery, thank you, Gandalf). I thought Gheist was mostly about helping Wraiths move on.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a Vampire being responsible for the creation of one or two of the ghosts that seek out Gheists, but not all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires and Sin-Eaters are most likely to conflict over persons of interest and locales of power. Sin-Eaters, Geists, and ghosts all have people who they rely on for resource reasons, nevermind the deeper and more cathartic investments, and when and where that crosses over with vampiric Touchstones and nodes of power/access, it can get messy. While haunted locations aren't of immediate interest to all vampires <i>for</i> their necrocosmic principles, a haunted place is a hell of a Haven, and whether yer cutting it by Clan or by Covenant, about 3 out of 5 of either of those have more personal reasons to have stake in such.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the obvious-vampires contribute to the dead frequently enough that it warrants some haunting, and that return of grievance can, in sufficient enough numbers, can incentivize a vampiric community to start favoring their mutations that lean into their role as...well, the dead, ie lean into those branches of the Kindred curses that tap into the necrocosmic.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh yeah, and also, the mundane resources that keep the lights going, the cults fed, and the cops out of your business are the sort of materials every supernatural fights over. Only so many people the deli owner or the senator can be in the pocket of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, it's not hard to see how some Krewes might react poorly to vampires-Furies who deal with systemic injustices tend to have opinions on monsters who kind of often thrive off of systemic corruption, as a minor example. Politics and theology are alive and well, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-14-2022, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T18:03:31-07:00","id":1484072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484069#post1484069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Gheist was mostly about helping Wraiths move on.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a Vampire being responsible for the creation of one or two of the ghosts that seek out Gheists, but not all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default game Geist is written for, as of 2e, is that you have your own Burden that drove you to accept the Bargain and return to the land of the living, your geist's Remembrance offering them the opportunity for catharsis so they can move on, and your krewe's fledgeling inquiries into the nature of life and death (and magic) as they work against the Underworld's system of suffering.<br /> <br /> The game's core conflict of Self vs Service is such that you can probably engineer some beef between a krewe trying to shift the meaning of death and a domain with a particularly high body count and degrading body disposal methods, but there's krewes of Bound (antagonists, in the base game) who've twisted their Bargains in their own favor and broken the will of their geists such that they'd get along just fine with the aforementioned Bastard Vampires and might instead get in trouble with, say, a ghost-savvy bloodline of Nosferatu. &quot;Ghosts are people, even if they're not actually the people they're made from&quot; is one of the theses of Geist, and a great many ghosts are <i>badly damaged</i> people just by virtue of their creation involving death or at least life-altering trauma.<br /> <br /> None of which really compares, as you note, to &quot;these people can be reasonably likened to dangerous magical animals who don't like the prospect of having to share hunting grounds even before any ideological conflict they have with each other.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T22:33:36-07:00","id":1484088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1483905#post1483905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Any vampire can learn without instructor Vigor (dots adds to Strenght), Resilience (dots adds to Stamina) and Celerity (dots adds to Defence).<br /> They cap at five dots, but extra levels can raise the relative attribute above the character normal cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want to know where is this stated because wherever I look Vigor, Resilience and Celerity are normal Disciplines for rules purpose. If you don't have that Discipline as a Clan Discipline, you need to drink Vitae from a vampire with that discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T00:13:02-07:00","id":1484089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484071#post1484071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires and Sin-Eaters are most likely to conflict over persons of interest and locales of power. Sin-Eaters, Geists, and ghosts all have people who they rely on for resource reasons, nevermind the deeper and more cathartic investments, and when and where that crosses over with vampiric Touchstones and nodes of power/access, it can get messy. While haunted locations aren't of immediate interest to all vampires <i>for</i> their necrocosmic principles, a haunted place is a hell of a Haven, and whether yer cutting it by Clan or by Covenant, about 3 out of 5 of either of those have more personal reasons to have stake in such.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the obvious-vampires contribute to the dead frequently enough that it warrants some haunting, and that return of grievance can, in sufficient enough numbers, can incentivize a vampiric community to start favoring their mutations that lean into their role as...well, the dead, ie lean into those branches of the Kindred curses that tap into the necrocosmic.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh yeah, and also, the mundane resources that keep the lights going, the cults fed, and the cops out of your business are the sort of materials every supernatural fights over. Only so many people the deli owner or the senator can be in the pocket of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, it's not hard to see how some Krewes might react poorly to vampires-Furies who deal with systemic injustices tend to have opinions on monsters who kind of often thrive off of systemic corruption, as a minor example. Politics and theology are alive and well, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, something more specific. I.e. Ordo Dracul occultists coteria tryed to study something Underworld related, and screw it up. <br /> And closest Krew is like:<br /> -What the fuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T01:28:13-07:00","id":1484095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484069#post1484069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure why Vampires and Sin Eaters would fight.<br /> <br /> Vampires and Werewolves both want the territory to hunt, even if for different prey. Vampires and Changelings both feed off people, even if in different ways. Magi want people to Awaken, which they can't do if they get turned into Vampires (they also really dig uncovering mysteries and Vampires like having their mystery, thank you, Gandalf). I thought Gheist was mostly about helping Wraiths move on.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a Vampire being responsible for the creation of one or two of the ghosts that seek out Gheists, but not all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to run the game with the assumption that none of the splats know that the others exist (individuals know, but not the splat as a whole). In this context, a Krewe might very well run into a Vampire tracking down what they think is a serial killer. This can lead to a very fun confrontation as the Vampire starts using Disciplines and the Krewe start using Haunts and both sides think &quot;What the hell is <i>that?</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T03:38:32-07:00","id":1484098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484088#post1484088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really want to know where is this stated because wherever I look Vigor, Resilience and Celerity are normal Disciplines for rules purpose. If you don't have that Discipline as a Clan Discipline, you need to drink Vitae from a vampire with that discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pag 83 of 2 ed core, it details how you can learn new discipline s dots","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T03:48:47-07:00","id":1484099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484046#post1484046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said there was a lot of chicanery.<br /> <br /> If you dig into the Werewolf merits you'll quickly find that the PU limits on attributes are at best guidelines. In this case to get 24 dice on the roll we have Stamina + Survival + Purity. Our stamina is 5 + 1 from favored form, +1 using totemic empowerment and +1 from either embodiment of the firstborn or the totem advantage. We'll activate the gift in either Urshul or Gauru for +2 stamina, bringing our stamina total to 10. We then add to that 5 Survival + 1 from totem advantages (so 6) plus 5 Purity plus willpower (3) gives us 24 dice total.<br /> <br /> Through similar chicanery our wolf has 6 brawl (plus area of expertise) and 7 strength going up to 8 in their favoured form (probably Gauru) before form bonuses. This all stacks along with the relevant Gifts to give us 24 dice as a base attack pool with however many successes * 2 extra dice from Crimson Spasm (I went with 7 as I said giving us 38).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There are a number of assumptions here I feel are unwarranted. For Force of Nature you've clearly assumed the Vampire has 5 Stamina and 5 Dex, I didn't assume this because it costs too much exp and the Vampire was already much more expensive than the Werewolf. If you want to spend another 12 exp getting the Vampire those attribute dots it puts him at 40 exp more expensive than the Werewolf and you have to reasonably start asking what the Werewolf is spending all that exp on (Tongue of Flame is always fun). And if you're going to be using force of nature, that that's 8 vitae and an instant action. Your BP 5 vampire only has 15 vitae and can only spend 5 per turn. In other words, that's 2 full turns before you can even start using the devotion, and then you need to spend <b>another</b> 2 instant actions to shift the dots around, and after all that you will only have 1 turn of full physical intensity blood boosting (assuming you spend blood on nothing else). I think it's fair to say that as your Vampire spends 4 turns &amp;quot;powering up&amp;quot; you're going to be absolutely eviscerated by the Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you're assuming a frenzy here. This I think is unwarranted. Vampires can't just choose to Frenzy (unlike Werewolves and Death Rage), and when they do Frenzy they can't choose what the Beast's goal is (and &amp;quot;get the fuck away from the big Werewolf&amp;quot; is more likely than &amp;quot;attack suicidally&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Even if we assume the Vampire is riding the wave, this can take several turns to activate and there's no guarantee that the check succeeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I ignored Swarm form since it doesn't directly boost the Vampire's dice pools and that was what I was most interested in. If we're going down that route though, Tongue of Flame is a hard counter to Swarm form. Also if you think about it Grasp of Howling winds should be devastating to a Vampire in Swarm form but obviously that's getting into the realm of ST fiat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's pretty clear that you can either have claws of the unholy OR swarm form but not both at the same time. Claws of the Unholy also isn't free, it requires frenzy, which leads to the issues described above. Furthermore, if you take Claws of the Unholy, that means you are not taking advantage of Protean 4's Barbed Hands meaning you lose the + Protean to grappling pools (meaning you lose grapples against the Werewolf and it can auto grapple you on a normal attack roll whenever it wishes). Lastly you're doing + 0 agg damage with claws of the unholy. Once you account for defense etc (be prepared for the Werewolf to have at least 12 defense) and things like Berserker's Might, you're going to be dealing very little if any damage</div> </div> </div> </div>About attributes assumptions, I assumed that also werewolf attributes were all max. <br /> <br /> About frenzy, frenzy is triggered by almost everything, also just simple verbal offenses, an angry werewolf is for sure enough of a threat to trigger frenzy. Tricky is to resist frenzy not let yourself fall to it.<br /> <br /> Nothing is preventing you to deal aggravated damages in swarm form: all protean transformations are cumulative, bats with claws (unholy claws) are still legit. Then you can houserule they are not because you think it's too OP, but don't call it as an hard rule.<br /> <br /> Defense 12 is not much of a deal when you roll 40 dice and have 5 automatic damages with Vigor. <br /> Talking about defense, and using all the book possibilities, there's also coil of the wyrm which add Blood Potency to health and defense. <br /> <br /> I think here we are getting back to a fandom debate between vampires vs werewolf to which I would rather abstain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T05:42:36-07:00","id":1484103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484099#post1484099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About attributes assumptions, I assumed that also werewolf attributes were all max. <br /> <br /> About frenzy, frenzy is triggered by almost everything, also just simple verbal offenses, an angry werewolf is for sure enough of a threat to trigger frenzy. Tricky is to resist frenzy not let yourself fall to it.<br /> <br /> Nothing is preventing you to deal aggravated damages in swarm form: all protean transformations are cumulative, bats with claws (unholy claws) are still legit. Then you can houserule they are not because you think it's too OP, but don't call it as an hard rule.<br /> <br /> Defense 12 is not much of a deal when you roll 40 dice and have 5 automatic damages with Vigor. <br /> Talking about defense, and using all the book possibilities, there's also coil of the wyrm which add Blood Potency to health and defense. <br /> <br /> I think here we are getting back to a fandom debate between vampires vs werewolf to which I would rather abstain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it possible to interrupt Swar attack with Hit-and-Run (Purity Facet of Evasion gift)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T06:12:04-07:00","id":1484105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484103#post1484103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it possible to interrupt Swar attack with Hit-and-Run (Purity Facet of Evasion gift)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hit and run is just to avoid an incoming attack if memory deserve, so I'd say no. And, in worst case scenario, would be contested by celerity.<br /> <br /> Edit: sorry I think I misunderstood what you meant. What do you mean with interrupting swarm attack? You can avoid the attack by moving away, yes. And yet will be contested by celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-15-2022, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T06:37:00-07:00","id":1484106,"title":"","content":"Since when? It not how dice pool is descrined for this Gift. The only thing I can get - add Celerety bonus to a vamp dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 06-15-2022, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T06:54:43-07:00","id":1484107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484106#post1484106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when? It not how dice pool is descrined for this Gift. The only thing I can get - add Celerety bonus to a vamp dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everytime two powers get into conflict it triggers a Clash of Willis. Celerity allows interrupts same way hit and run does. So vampire can try to interrupt werewolf's attempts to &quot;interrupt&quot; running away which is a clear clash of wills: <br /> Would be celerity+Blood Potency vs werewolf's Primal urge+purity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T08:31:40-07:00","id":1484111,"title":"","content":"Ok, then. I got this. Something the one can work with.<br /> Speaking of - the biggest Uratha problem - they are to slow. Literally 2.5 pretty minor 'spidster'abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 06-15-2022, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T09:28:29-07:00","id":1484113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484111#post1484111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, then. I got this. Something the one can work with.<br /> Speaking of - the biggest Uratha problem - they are to slow. Literally 2.5 pretty minor 'spidster'abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too slow?<br /> <br /> Uratha in Urhan and Urshul forms have +5 and +7 speed respectively. Urhan has an ability like Celerity's active effect built into the form. They don't have anything to match the single-turn speed of high Celerity, but by combining the forms with Predator's Unmatched Pursuit they can easily be moving at 25+ speed every turn for a scene, doubling that to 50 speed for 1 essence, or for free in Kuruth.<br /> <br /> You also have to consider that if you're seriously intent on running from a Werewolf you're going to end up in a foot chase. In a foot chase, you'll be rolling Stamina + Athletics, while the Urhan will be rolling its speed pool, which as I mentioned can be in the 50s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T11:45:28-07:00","id":1484124,"title":"","content":"Lets look at how vampires and other splats can shape the battlefield to suit their needs. Werewolves can use their abilities to infiltrate and, for example, seal off all exits. But how do changelings go about it ? What are the logistical and tactical differences infiltrating the base of a Geist krewe over a Mage cabal ? What are the general outlines of the dynamic plays and counterplays the vampires and their opponents can expect ? What supernaturally prepared defenses would a vampire's compound have ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-15-2022, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T12:30:29-07:00","id":1484125,"title":"","content":"Aside from a few haunts like the rage (burst aggravated damage and automatic negative tilts could make short work of a vamp) and the caul, most of the sin eaters haunts are situational and more geared toward dealing with ghosts in general rather than fighting, they are a little harder to kill compared to normal human beings but not by that much, plasmic healing is very expensive and generally used in the aftermath of a confrontation, killing them permanently is a pain in the ass (especially since, unless you know a geist bane or kill the sin eater in a way they died originally, the geist is going to be unleashed and you will have to kill it too to prevent the sin eater resurrection) but definitely not impossible, especially for werewolves since bound geists don't have the same stats of an unbound geist of the same rank (don't know why) so even a single werewolf (especially if they have the barghest facet) shouldn't have that difficult of a time sealing the deal. Regarding krewe tactics, it really depends from the krewe and their members, ghost members are very useful information gatherer and spies and some of the krewe rituals (which can be done by anyone, even humans) are pretty damn good but aside from that, a krewe relies mainly on mundane resources and connections to keep functioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 06-15-2022, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T15:10:56-07:00","id":1484141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484125#post1484125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but definitely not impossible, especially for werewolves since bound geists don't have the same stats of an unbound geist of the same rank (don't know why) so even a single werewolf (especially if they have the barghest facet) shouldn't have that difficult of a time sealing the deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure where the werewolves come into this discussion, considering the topic is about the interactions between vampires and other splats and therefore the ability of werewolves to deal with a Rank 3 ghost with access to Haunts is kind of irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main thing vampires have angling for them in a conflict with other splats is the same opportunistic approach to supernatural power that they take to mundane power \u2014 like mages, vampires as a whole are kind of incentivized to be magpies* about things they can put to use for their own purposes, even as bloodlines and territorial pressures encourage them to settle on a niche; like the Web of Pain, they tend to be connected enough that a route exists for any given one of them to pull on the potentially diverse resources of another, whether that's legal, political, criminal, occult, or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* or a crow. or an owl. something avian, at least.</span><br /> <br /> It's possible that a given domain simply doesn't have any vampires who've taken an interest in phenomena that can give a pack/cabal/throng/motley/cell/krewe/meret/ring/cohort a hard time, in which case the more dimensionally savvy side wins unless they trip over mundane defenses and vampiric powers, but vampires who've survived though encounters with unusual monsters have an incentive to ensure that they do so again. It's the old vampires-as-institutional-corruption saw of &quot;better completely wipe them out if you don't want them to come back fifteen years later with acquired immunity to Agent Orange&quot; at work, and the variety of magical weirdness in the Chronicles of Darkness that isn't locked to another world can as easily be turned on other monsters as mortals and vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T17:36:11-07:00","id":1484156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484141#post1484141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The main thing vampires have angling for them in a conflict with other splats is the same opportunistic approach to supernatural power that they take to mundane power \u2014 like mages, vampires as a whole are kind of incentivized to be magpies* about things they can put to use for their own purposes, even as bloodlines and territorial pressures encourage them to settle on a niche; like the Web of Pain, they tend to be connected enough that a route exists for any given one of them to pull on the potentially diverse resources of another, whether that's legal, political, criminal, occult, or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a certain inclination myself to think that in a supernatural conflict, a vampire prince is a bit more likely to rally the domain's resources towards dealing with a severe threat to one of its members that they're judged to have not had coming (and maybe a few that do) than many other supernatural societies are to come to the defence of their constituents. I have a preference for picturing mage cabals as holding one another at arms length a bit more and the Consilium isn't really built to be a system that rallies to defence (other than issuing general warnings and maybe maintaining a few wards against particularly dangerous mysteries) unless they're mages of enemy sects, and werewolves have that whole thing where packs are just as likely to eye one another up for a fight. Most of the others seem a bit too sparse or subtle anyway, although I have a suspicion that changelings might be able to work along similar lines.<br /> <br /> Part of that is at least to give the top office of a vampire place a role to distinguish itself a bit if it's going to be there. That a lot of vampires might not like submitting in fealty, but it's hard to not admit the benefits when there's somebody who seems able to direct a lot of the power and resources of your fellows to your aid when it's really needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-15T22:35:52-07:00","id":1484178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1483900-are-vampires-weak?p=1484141#post1484141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure where the werewolves come into this discussion, considering the topic is about the interactions between vampires and other splats and therefore the ability of werewolves to deal with a Rank 3 ghost with access to Haunts is kind of irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main thing vampires have angling for them in a conflict with other splats is the same opportunistic approach to supernatural power that they take to mundane power \u2014 like mages, vampires as a whole are kind of incentivized to be magpies* about things they can put to use for their own purposes, even as bloodlines and territorial pressures encourage them to settle on a niche; like the Web of Pain, they tend to be connected enough that a route exists for any given one of them to pull on the potentially diverse resources of another, whether that's legal, political, criminal, occult, or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* or a crow. or an owl. something avian, at least.</span><br /> <br /> It's possible that a given domain simply doesn't have any vampires who've taken an interest in phenomena that can give a pack/cabal/throng/motley/cell/krewe/meret/ring/cohort a hard time, in which case the more dimensionally savvy side wins unless they trip over mundane defenses and vampiric powers, but vampires who've survived though encounters with unusual monsters have an incentive to ensure that they do so again. It's the old vampires-as-institutional-corruption saw of &amp;quot;better completely wipe them out if you don't want them to come back fifteen years later with acquired immunity to Agent Orange&amp;quot; at work, and the variety of magical weirdness in the Chronicles of Darkness that isn't locked to another world can as easily be turned on other monsters as mortals and vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. We're talking about vamps vs other splats, right?<br /> Speaking of - what a geist can do against vampire with all things equal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T01:51:57-07:00","id":1484185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com